<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/languages>
    a logic:Ontology ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow> ;
    rdfs:comment "Languages and writing systems as first-class, registry-INDEPENDENT information objects (the BCP-47 / ISO 639 / Glottolog / Wikidata / schema.org superset layer). A gmeow:Language has a self-minted IRI; codes (gmeow:languageCode, gmeow:authorityLink, skos:exactMatch) are OPTIONAL alignments, never identity — so a code-less conlang (Ithkuil), a fast-versioning AI-minted interlingua, an under-coded sign/minority language, and a programming language are all co-equal first-class languages. Covers natural, constructed (auxiliary/engineered/artistic/ritual), AI-generated, historical/reconstructed, sign/whistled/tactile, and formal/programming/markup languages. Writing systems are grounded in the lang: layer: a script is a lang:Script (character repertoire) and the convention binding a language to a script is a lang:Orthography (lang:orthographyFor + lang:usesScript), so a language CO-MINGLES many co-equal scripts (Japanese = kanji/Hani + hiragana/Hira + katakana/Kana + rōmaji/Latn) as several co-equal orthographies. Versions form a first-class lineage (gmeow:versionOf / supersedes). Endonym/exonym names reuse the names module's gmeow:Appellation; transliteration schemes that produce a gmeow:romanization are named by gmeow:transliterationScheme and catalogued as FnO functions in the projection layer."@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/languages> ;
    rdfs:label "GMEOW Languages Module"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The GMEOW Languages Module — classes, properties, and individuals of the GMEOW super-vocabulary."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxConfigBox ,
        gmeow:boxTBox .

# ── logic: assertion carriers for this slice's own terms ────────────────────────
# The canonical logic: carriers for the characteristics and integrity conditions of the
# terms THIS slice owns. Each record names one of this slice's own properties or classes
# through a logic: RBox predicate; the native coherence gate joins the record to enforce
# the condition, and the OWL grounding view projects OWL FunctionalProperty (and friends)
# from it. Authored here rather than in the logic slice because the fact asserted is a
# fact about this slice's own term, and a grounding slice never depends on a non-grounding
# slice (docs/GROUNDING.md, the tier rule): the logic: assertion vocabulary is CONSUMED
# here (gmeow:sliceDependsOn logic), never owned.
#   logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion — logic:characterizes names the property, logic:characteristicSort its characteristic.

gmeow:proficiencyAgentFunctionality
    a logic:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/languages> ;
    rdfs:label "proficiencyAgent is functional"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:proficiencyAgent is functional: a language-proficiency relator expresses the proficiency of exactly one agent, the identity-constituting party whose command of the language the reified proficiency is about. This record is not a definition of that term and never a shape: the obligation is reasoned from the record, not restated elsewhere."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:characterizes gmeow:proficiencyAgent ;
    logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:proficiencyAgent ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when the native coherence gate must enforce that gmeow:proficiencyAgent names exactly one value; this record is the canonical carrier the gate joins, so the obligation is reasoned rather than restated on a shape surface."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid this record when a second value would make the record ambiguous — retire the assertion instead of weakening it, and never mirror it as a hand-authored shape."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Read together with logic:characteristicSort: the pair (logic:characterizes gmeow:proficiencyAgent, logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty) is the whole obligation, and the OWL grounding view projects the matching characteristic from it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: this record carries ONE integrity obligation about gmeow:proficiencyAgent and nothing else. It is not a definition of gmeow:proficiencyAgent (that lives on the term itself), not a shape, and not a second place to state the term's meaning — retire the record rather than broaden it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "gmeow:proficiencyAgentFunctionality logic:characterizes gmeow:proficiencyAgent ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox .
